<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Rugby League-ARL appoints Whittaker as chief executive.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Rugby League-ARL appoints Whittaker as chief executive.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Australian Rugby League (ARL) has appointed Balmain club president Neil Whittaker as the ruling body's new chief executive to replace John Quayle.</p>
<p>Whittaker played for Balmain as a hooker between 1979 and 1985. Quayle stepped down last month after more than a decade in the job.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373 1800</p>
</text>
